error[E0277]: `DoubleWord<*mut u64, *mut u64>` lends no place of its own
  --> tests/compile_fail/raw_access_to_two_words.rs:17:18
   |
17 |     let _ = pair.as_ptr();
   |                  ^^^^^^ expected a primitive other than a `DoubleWord`
   |
   = help: the trait `RawAccess` is not implemented for `DoubleWord<*mut u64, *mut u64>`
   = note: a double word's cell holds each pointer's address, its provenance exposed, so a pointer read through a place would have none: reach two words through `load`, `store` and the compare-exchanges
   = help: the following other types implement trait `RawAccess`:
             *mut T
             bool
             i128
             i16
             i32
             i64
             i8
             isize
           and $N others
note: required by a bound in `atomix_core::Atomic::<T>::as_ptr`
  --> src/atomic/mod.rs
   |
   | impl<T: Atom> Atomic<T> {
...
   |     pub const fn as_ptr(&self) -> *mut T::Repr
   |     where
   |         T::Repr: [const] RawAccess,
   |                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `Atomic::<T>::as_ptr`

error[E0277]: an atomic of `(NonNull<u64>, NonNull<u64>)` shares no place with a `(NonNull<u64>, NonNull<u64>)`
  --> tests/compile_fail/raw_access_to_two_words.rs:18:18
   |
18 |     let _ = pair.get_mut();
   |                  ^^^^^^^ expected `bool`, an integer or a `*mut` pointer to a sized value
   |
   = help: the trait `atomix_core::__private::RawValue` is not implemented for `(NonNull<u64>, NonNull<u64>)`
   = note: an atomic's place is its value's only where the value is its own repr, every one of which decodes
   = note: an atomic of any other value reaches it through `&mut` with `get`, `set` and `with_mut`
